  "items": [
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "After 3 days of dialogue, the Democratic Republic of Congo and Rwanda sign a provisional peace treaty and are set to begin negotiations for a draft peace treaty on June 27. ((Al Jazeera))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "The death toll from Israel's strikes on Iran rises to more than 240, including 70 women and children. To date, at least 24 people have been killed by Iranian strikes on Israel. ((Al Jazeera))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Iran strikes four sites in central and southern Israel. The Soroka Medical Center in Beersheba, is hit by an Iranian ballistic missile, injuring at least 240 people. Iran says it was targeting a military site, striking an Israeli military and intelligence centre located near the hospital. ((Al Jazeera)) ((AP))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "The Israeli Air Force strikes the Arak Nuclear Complex, a heavy-water reactor near Arak, Iran. ((The Times of Israel))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Israeli gunfire and airstrikes kill at least 92 Palestinians across the Gaza Strip, including 16 people waiting for aid assistance near the Netzarim Corridor. ((Al Jazeera))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "A rockslide at Bow Glacier Falls near Banff, Alberta, Canada, kills at least one person and injures or kills several others. ((Calgary Herald)) ((CFCN-DT)) ((Global News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "International relations",
      "text": "A hand grenade is thrown into the courtyard of the residence of the Norwegian ambassador to Israel in Herzliya. ((Reuters))"
    },
    {
      "category": "International relations",
      "text": "The Finnish Parliament votes 155–18 to withdraw from the Ottawa Treaty, which bans the use of anti-personnel mines, citing the threat Russia poses to its national security. ((Reuters)) ((Helsingin Sanomat))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "After three days of dialogue, the Democratic Republic of the Congo and Rwanda sign a provisional peace treaty and are set to begin negotiations for a draft peace treaty on June 27. ((Al Jazeera))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "A rockslide at Bow Glacier Falls near Banff, Alberta, Canada, kills at least two people. Three other hikers sustained injuries. ((CFCN-DT))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Law and crime",
      "text": "A federal appeals court rules that President of the United States Donald Trump is allowed to keep the National Guard under federal control in California, pending further litigation. ((BBC News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Law and crime",
      "text": "The Rwandan government arrests opposition figure Victoire Ingabire Umuhoza, founder of the United Democratic Forces, for allegedly plotting to incite public unrest. ((AP)) ((RFI))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "Four people are missing after a Kawasaki medical helicopter on a rescue operation crashes north of Baie-Johan-Beetz near Natashquan on the Côte-Nord in Quebec, Canada. The pilot is found and taken to hospital. ((CBC))"
    }
  ],
